 ### UI (In-game)
 
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5531+) **Beautified** and **expanded**, and add **support for text upscaling** for miscallenous **screens**: [CvDawnOfMan.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDawnOfMan.py) ("The sun rises on the Year" greeting new game screen) is **expanded laterally and vertically** to **avoid scrolling**, add **icons** for buildings and units, add icon **chars for traits**; [CvTechSplashScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechSplashScreen.py) (when a new tech is discovered)  is moderately **expanded** to **avoid scrolling**, vertically center screen (was slightly excentered); [CvHallOfFameScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvHallOfFameScreen.py) is **maximized to full screen** with enlarged columns, and **new Leader, Civilization, Player Color, and Traits columns** with **icons** or **colors** or **chars** (based on Info Screen's Score tab: note that Civilization icon is approximative and will not work if Civilization name is not the base civ mod name (e.g. "The United States" -> "My American Custom Name Empire") (would add too much complexity in DLL for a working UI feature outside this edge case); note 2: trait info is indicative only (if traits in XML were different when the save file was made (e.g., expansive trait removed, leader trait allocation changed), this information will be lost)); [CvReplayScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvReplayScreen.py) is **maximized to full screen**; [CvDanQuayle.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDanQuayle.py) ("you have displayed the leadership abilities" post-game screen) is **maximized to full screen** and has a **greatly expanded leader NIF** and **maximized vertically score table** to **avoid scrolling**. See [README.md (Miscallenous screens)](/README.md#miscallenous-screens)
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5517+) **Reorganized advisors**: **merged** the **espionage** screen into the **Foreign Advisor**, the **Economic Advisor's Finance Tab** into the **Domestic Advisor**, moved away the **Environment Tab** from the former **Economic Advisor** (now removed), the **Religion** Advisor and **Corporation** Advisor (so it is always visible and easier to access) into the new **Policy Advisor**; so they are now **tabs of these instead** (deleted the old now obsolete lone advisor .py files); **swap advisors**: **Victory screen** to F9 and **Info Screen** to F8 so the Info Screen is easier to split to F7 and F8 later on and so layout is **more logically organized** from internal to external advisors; **split advisors**: the **Foreign Advisor** is now split into **Foreign Trade Advisor (F4)** (TREATIES, BONUSES, TECHS, CITIES), and **Foreign Diplomacy Advisor (F3)** (RELATIONS, GLANCE, INFO, ESPIONAGE) as it **was crowded** to reduce the need for **tab navigation** and for **clearer thematic differentiation**, using a shell (i.e. almost empty file for **linking only**) [CvForeignDiplomacyAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignDiplomacyAdvisor.py) file for the 2nd advisor.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5524+) Rearrange Advisor **keyboard shortcuts** (in [CIV4ControlInfos.xml](/Assets/XML/Units/CIV4ControlInfos.xml) and DLL files like [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvGameInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvGameInterface.cpp), and [CyEnumsInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CyEnumsInterface.cpp)) and adjust the **order of advisor buttons** in map view and **Sevopedia shortcuts** corresponding text to match the advisors changes.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5754+) Add **debug mode support** (for player selection) in the Domestic Advisor. Add **Barbarian** to **selectable leaders** in debug mode in advisors where it is relevant: Domestic Advisor, Policy Advisor, World Advisor, and Info Screen.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5859+) Preserve **selected debug/vassal perspective** when reopening or switching tabs in supported advisors where the selected player is meaningful (all supported advisors except for the Victory Screen's **Settings tab**: it intentionally stays anchored to the **real active player**, because it describes that player's game setup rather than a selected rival's victory progress).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5755) Allow the **current active player**'s (i.e. the human player or whichever player is active if cheats are enabled) to **select and view its alive vassals' information** in advisors' **player selection dropdown** even outside debug mode. This follows the active player (vassals are subordinate enough to make their domestic/world/policy state relevant). This **does not reveal unrelated players or hidden map** data as debug mode would.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5859+) Preserve built heavy **advisor tables** across same-advisor **tab switches** and screen **close/reopen** where worthwhile: Military Advisor's **Battles** table and Info Screen's **Timeline** table. This especially improves loading when hundreds of rows are stored. Rebuild when player/history/language/layout or relevant display settings change. This is partly based on the **Technology Advisor's persistent-screen pattern**, which notably preserves scroll position on reopen.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5521+) **Expand** and most **advisors** so they scale to **game resolution dynamically** instead of hardcoded advisor screen dimensions. The code was also refactored to improve **dynamic scaling**, ensuring **most UI elements automatically realign** if dimensions are changed. Advisors are now **excentered** so **overall more information** is displayed, thus **reducing the need for scrolling**, while still **preserving key relevant information** for display (scoreboard, map, commerce sliders and values, etc.). Some of their dimensions are **harmonized**. Note: some **right space for scoreboard** and **top space for the top bars** of the main interface was made (since commerce sliders are now as of now on the right side, they don't need left space anymore). See [Main Advisors reworks](/README.md#main-advisors-reworks-eg-overview-tabs-domestic-advisor-new-world-advisor-score-tab-and-timeline-tab-info-screen).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5771+) Make some of the data-dense advisors use using a **higher constrast background theme** so text is **more readable** (e.g. plain dark grayish in Overview tabs (Domestic Advisor), plain dark brownish in the Score tab (Info screen), plain blue in the Battles tab (Military Advisor)).
-- **Beautified** the **Domestic Advisor**: now shows the **button (i.e. icon) of the current item being built** (unit, building, project, process) in "Producing" column. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) Use the **shared advisor shell layout** (**top/bottom bars** + single content panel, remove the old exit icon) so Domestic Advisor **mirrors other advisors' structure** instead of a floating table, (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5753+) and is now has **tabs**; **enhanced** the Domestic Advisor so it now has **4 overview tabs** with detailed city information (modifiers, yields, specialists, etc.) with a corresponding **legend link**, and an **enter city on click button** (mirroring the info screen's wonders tab). Change in [CvDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDomesticAdvisor.py).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5528+) Minor **beautified** the [CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvCustomizableDomesticAdvisor.py): increase **legend culture text width** so it is not cramped when upscaled. Note: although it is functional, the Custom Domestic Advisor is **not supported** in AdvCiv-SAS as of now, so it is lacking the Finance Tab. See also [KI#123](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#123---fixed-bug-domesticmilitary-advisor-variant-toggles-required-restarting-civ4).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5522+) New **Policy Advisor**. **Beautified**: enlarge **top panels text** so **long civic names don't overflow**. **Remove multiline nationality** information which was **uninfomative** and **crowded vertically** in the **Religions tab** and the **Corporations tab**; use more precise and compact `Leader (ID)` and `HQ (ID)` **one-liner instead** (**ID** also handles **one leader name being used by several players**); **increase row spacing** (now **unified** (was crowded)). **Remove multiline wrapped bonuses** splitting logic in the **Corporations tab**: use one natural comma-separated line (bonuses row height reduced/standardized) since there is enough space after expanding the Policy Advisor and it is more readable. Also add **new rows** (**Bonuses Generated**, **Yields Generated**), and add **first column descriptions** for rows (as of now `Built By:`, `Consumes:`, `Generates:`, `Generates 2:`). Add a **Great Person icon** in `Built By:` row. Change in [CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvPolicyAdvisorScreen.py).
-- **Foreign Advisor**: refined its tabs so they can display **up to 12 players**. Notably renamed the Active tab to **Treaties** tab (no longer shows redundant bonuses (since their deal can be cancelled from the bonuses tab)), and **beautified** it with **icons**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5516+) Always use the unified **table-style info layout** (`drawInfoImproved`) for the Info Tab for stable column behavior: the old hardcoded text spacing (`drawInfoOriginal`) did not **scale with upscaled font text** nor **adjust depending on advisor screen size**. Plus the improved layout has additional **information** like general or specific **colored leader attitude text** related to civic/religion choices (e.g., `[-2]` or `[+1]`). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5518+) **Beautified** the **Espionage Tab** similarly; notably **removed redundant Espionage slider** now that commerce sliders are on the right side of main interface in map view, and **improved text spacing** that **was colliding or overflowing** beyond its panel, and **moved + - buttons under the leader icon** where there is more room and it is more intuitive and easier to click it. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5793+) Show **gold per turn** in **Bonuses Tab** even when **not connected to trade network** (if gold trading is available): previously this was hidden, and would require tediously opening the diplomacy screen of each player, and this is now also consistent with flat gold being shown in techs tab for all players (if gold trading is available). See [KI#132](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#132---enhanced-base-advciv-issue-of-not-showing-rival-gold-per-turn-on-foreign-trade-advisor-bonuses-tab-when-not-connected-to-their-trade-network).
-- Added **"Willing to become vassal"** and **"Vassal"** **icons** in the Foreign Advisor's Glance tab in the human player's row, to help avoid the need to tediously check these up through other screens, in [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py), and in [CvDLLWidgetData.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDLLWidgetData.cpp) for the corresponding **tooltip** (on hover). See ["Willing to become a vassal" and "vassal" icons](/README.md#willing-to-become-a-vassal-and-vassal-icons-in-foreign-advisors-glance-tab). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5808+) Cap **maximum number of players per page** in the **Glance Tab** (e.g., max 16 players per page gives 3 pages at SAS48 Worldsize (if all players are known)), with **clickable left and right arrows for navigation**. Fixes **issue of Glance Tab clipping horizontally** if more than 24 players are known and columns being too tight. Last page visited is **remembered and resumed from** on Glance Tab next opening. See [KI#134](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#134---fixed-base-advciv-issue-foreign-diplomacy-advisor-glance-tab-column-icons-overflow-horizontally-with-24-rival-players).
-- Reworked the **Military Advisor** in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) now with Unit Combat and Units **icons**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5530+) Note: **unit icon size** is **increased** at **higher resolutions** (e.g., from 24 to 32 if resolution height >= 1440), and **promotion icon size** is **increased** (no longer DLL-hardcoded (was 16)). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5777+) **Lift up the unit panel to full height** (reduces the need for scrolling vertically) and **expand it laterally** to **accomodate lengthy unit rows** (e.g., avoid line wrap if unit name is long, if there are many promotions). Make **show/hide individual unit text clickable** too (more accessible than the small +/- button alone). **Increase leader icon bar from 1 to multiple rows**, and **do not reduce icon size until all rows are full**. For example, at 1080p, 5 rows allow to show up to 45 players (including barbarian) at full leader icon size before leader icon size is reduced. **Reduce Leader icon size reduction** when all rows are full (**mild reduction**, no longer halved). See also [KI#123](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#123---fixed-bug-domesticmilitary-advisor-variant-toggles-required-restarting-civ4), [KI#130](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#130---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-unit-rows-showing-build-player-name-instead-of-improvement-text-military-advisor-map-tab), and [KI#131](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#131---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-live-unit-build-action-text-not-being-space-separated-from-its-turn-timer). Note 2: as of now the [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) is not supported.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5771+) Added a new **Battles tab** in the Military Advisor, showing as a **sortable table** the detailed **record of each battle** for the selected player in debug dropdown (or the active player or its vassals outside debug mode): **Turn**, **Year**, **Result** (Won, Lost, Retreat) as emoji, **Estimated Odds %** (simple starting effective strength comparison, not exact Civ4 combat odds), **Role** (Are we the attacker?) as emoji, **base Strength** (XML), **start effective Strength** (including modifiers at that battle), **end effective Strength**, **max effective Strength**, **XP before combat** (yellow if Great-General-led), **Our Unit**, **Their Unit** (unit name in yellow if Great-General-led), **same** strength/XP columns for their unit, **Civ icon**, **Player icon**, **Player ID** (to cover the same leader picked by several leaders (custom games, etc.)), **Captured Unit type**, **Captured Unit icon**, **Hill or Peak icon**, **Terrain icon**, **Feature icon**, **Click Plot icon** (**on click camera is moved to this plot** (as the wonder tabs' (Info Screen) text does), with distinct art for normal plot, defended city, and captured city battles). Icons are **hoverable to sevopedia** (or have a camera effect). **Text color** is added for Result (Won: green; Lost: red; Retreat: yellow), effective Strength (white: 100%, green: > 66%, yellow: > 33%; red <= 33%), and captured units (we gained a unit amount: green; we lost a unit amout: red). Implemented a **legend link**, and **LOG Button** (as the Timeline tab). Examples of LOG: `163 | 760 AD | Lost | 43 | A | 6 | 6.04 |  | 7.20 | 8 | 0 | Camel Archer | Longbowman | 5 | 0 | 4 | 8.10 | 5.04 | 9.00 | 9 | 0 |  |  | TERRAIN_GRASS |  | 54 | 30`, `133 | 10 BC | Won | 64 | A | 3 | 3.30 | 1.81 | 3.30 | 2 | 0 | Trireme | Galley | 1 | 0 | 2 | 1.84 |  | 2.20 | 48 | 0 |  |  | TERRAIN_COAST |  | 32 | 10`. Main files changed: [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py), [SASBattleHistory.py](/Assets/Python/SASBattleHistory.py), [CvEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/CvEventManager.py), [BugEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/BugEventManager.py), [CvUnit.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvUnit.cpp), [CvDllPythonEvents.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDllPythonEvents.cpp), [CvDllPythonEvents.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDllPythonEvents.h), [CvEventReporter.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEventReporter.cpp), [CvEventReporter.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEventReporter.h).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5802+) Added a new **Summary tab** in the Military Advisor, showing a **synthetic view** of our Military: **Support** (detailed Cost and Supply, and Unit Cap numerical breakdown (e.g., `P x R x M    (1 x 100 x 82) / 10000 = 0 gold icon char`), Military Buildings, Military Production (some not shown for concision as panel is mostly full) and XP information, and Allied Hammers for total hammer value of allies' (e.g., vassals, same team) army); **Army** (detailed numerical overview for military/civilian units, Domain repartition (Land/Sea/Air), Strongest, Costliest, Total/Avg Hammers as a power estimatation of units, Power Rank (Known) (e.g., `9/11` (in fact `44/48` if debug mode is enabled for spoilers)), Top promotions, Covert Units (Invisible, Spies, Hidden Nationality), And upgradeable units costs (Min/Avg/Max/Total)); **Deployment** (Allied/Neutral/Enemy Cities/Territory/Roaming information with Avg Defense and Best defense of our cities, defensive buildings (as of now Walls and Castles (e.g., `1 / 2`)), Wounded information (Max/Avg/Min and Full/High/Medium/Low Health (e.g, `15 (100%)`)), and Battles reusing the [SASBattleHistory.py](/Assets/Python/SASBattleHistory.py) added with the new Battles Tab (Won/Retreated/Lost (e.g., `35 (33%)`)), Good-Luck Wins and Bad-Luck Losses counts (`e.g., 11 (31%)`), Best/Worst (e.g., `6.3 vs 10.0 1300 AD (39%)`)). Also added a **legend link**.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5775+) Added a new **Composition Tab**, as a set of **sortable tables** for **Current** (unlike saved data in the Statistics Tab in the Info Screen) **Units** (non-civilian, including Animal (including Barbarian in debug mode)), **Promotions**, and **Unit Combats** **counts**, default-**sorted from most to least** for no tedium (as done in the Statistics Tab). See also [KI#129](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#129---fixed-military-advisor-map-tab-minimap-disappeared-after-switching-tabs).
-- Similarly Beautified and Enhanced the **Technology Advisor** in [CvTechChooser.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechChooser.py) so it uses more of the screen while still preserving key information. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5519+) Players can **optionally** set an **alternative lower right space for scoreboard** on **lower game resolutions** (e.g., 1920*1080) so that an **extra column or more is visible** in the technology advisor, and an **alternative top space space** for **advisor buttons** (in map view) because this alternative right space may cover these advisor buttons. **Boldened title** for consistency. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5520+) See also [KI#114](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#114---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-tech-advisor-on-save-load-initially-shown-current-tech-missing-turns-left-timer-until-another-tech-is-clicked). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5691+) **When opening** Technology Advisor, **right-align scoreboard leader text** so it is easier to read (because text is often not visible due to advisor width expansion). **On Technology Advisor close**, it **reverts back** to usual alignment.
+- **Beautified** and **expanded**, and add **support for text upscaling** for miscellaneous **screens**: [CvDawnOfMan.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDawnOfMan.py) ("The sun rises on the Year" greeting new game screen) is **expanded laterally and vertically** to **avoid scrolling**, add **icons** for buildings and units, add icon **chars for traits**; [CvTechSplashScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechSplashScreen.py) (when a new tech is discovered)  is moderately **expanded** to **avoid scrolling**, vertically center screen (was slightly excentered); [CvHallOfFameScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvHallOfFameScreen.py) is **maximized to full screen** with enlarged columns, and **new Leader, Civilization, Player Color, and Traits columns** with **icons** or **colors** or **chars** (based on Info Screen's Score Tab: note that Civilization icon is approximative and will not work if Civilization name is not the base civ mod name (e.g. "The United States" -> "My American Custom Name Empire") (would add too much complexity in DLL for a working UI feature outside this edge case); note 2: trait info is indicative only (if traits in XML were different when the save file was made (e.g., expansive trait removed, leader trait allocation changed), this information will be lost)); [CvReplayScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvReplayScreen.py) is **maximized to full screen**; [CvDanQuayle.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvDanQuayle.py) ("you have displayed the leadership abilities" post-game screen) is **maximized to full screen** and has a **greatly expanded leader NIF** and **maximized vertically score table** to **avoid scrolling**. See [README.md (Miscellaneous screens)](/README.md#miscellaneous-screens)
+- **Reorganized advisors**: **merged** the **espionage** screen into the **Foreign Advisor**, the **Economic Advisor's Finance Tab** into the **Domestic Advisor**, moved away the **Environment Tab** from the former **Economic Advisor** (now removed), the **Religion** Advisor and **Corporation** Advisor (so it is always visible and easier to access) into the new **Policy Advisor**; so they are now **tabs of these instead** (deleted the old now obsolete lone advisor .py files); **swap advisors**: **Victory screen** to F9 and **Info Screen** to F8 so the Info Screen is easier to split to F7 and F8 later on and so layout is **more logically organized** from internal to external advisors; **split advisors**: the **Foreign Advisor** is now split into **Foreign Trade Advisor (F4)** (TREATIES, BONUSES, TECHS, CITIES), and **Foreign Diplomacy Advisor (F3)** (RELATIONS, GLANCE, INFO, ESPIONAGE) as it **was crowded** to reduce the need for **tab navigation** and for **clearer thematic differentiation**, using a shell (i.e. almost empty file for **linking only**) [CvForeignDiplomacyAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignDiplomacyAdvisor.py) file for the 2nd advisor.
+- Rearrange Advisor **keyboard shortcuts** (in [CIV4ControlInfos.xml](/Assets/XML/Units/CIV4ControlInfos.xml) and DLL files like [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvEnums.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEnums.h), [CvGameInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvGameInterface.cpp), and [CyEnumsInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CyEnumsInterface.cpp)) and adjust the **order of advisor buttons** in map view and **Sevopedia shortcuts** corresponding text to match the advisors changes.
