+- Preserve **selected debug/vassal perspective** when reopening or switching tabs in supported advisors where the selected player is meaningful (all supported advisors except for the Victory Screen's **Settings tab**: it intentionally stays anchored to the **real active player**, because it describes that player's game setup rather than a selected rival's victory progress).
+- Allow the **current active player** (i.e. the human player or whichever player is active if cheats are enabled) to **select and view its alive vassals' information** in advisors' **player selection dropdown** even outside debug mode. This follows the active player (vassals are subordinate enough to make their domestic/world/policy state relevant). This **does not reveal unrelated players or hidden map** data as debug mode would.
+- Always show advisor tabs where hidden tabs reduced discoverability: Foreign Advisor **Glance** and **Cities** tabs are now always shown, so the corresponding old BUG menu visibility toggles are now removed; Victory Screen **Resolutions** and **Members** tabs are also always shown, with a fallback table showing required wonders (as of now Apostolic Palace or United Nations) when no vote source is currently active.
+- Preserve built heavy **advisor tables** where safe, to avoid rebuilding expensive UI tables when their player/history/language/layout/settings signature has not changed. This is used for the **Info Screen Timeline** table across close/reopen, and for the **Military Advisor Battles** table across **same-open advisor tab switches** (Map <-> Battles/Summary/Composition remains lightweight as long as the Military Advisor is not exited). We deliberately do **not** preserve the whole Military Advisor across full close/reopen: testing `screen.setPersistent(True)` there made very large late-game Battles histories faster to reopen, but broke Civ4's native minimap lifecycle, causing the Map tab to reopen as an empty blue panel and also break after debug-mode transitions until save reload. So the Battles cache is kept for tab switching only, while full Military Advisor close/reopen rebuilds the screen/minimap for reliability. See also [KI#129](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#129---fixed-military-advisor-map-tab-minimap-disappeared-after-switching-tabs).
