nected to trade network** (if gold trading is available): previously this was hidden, and would require tediously opening the diplomacy screen of each player, and this is now also consistent with flat gold being shown in techs tab for all players (if gold trading is available). See [KI#132](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#132---enhanced-base-advciv-issue-of-not-showing-rival-gold-per-turn-on-foreign-trade-advisor-bonuses-tab-when-not-connected-to-their-trade-network).
+- Added **"Willing to become vassal"** and **"Vassal"** **icons** in the Foreign Advisor's Glance tab in the human player's row, to help avoid the need to tediously check these up through other screens, in [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py), and in [CvDLLWidgetData.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDLLWidgetData.cpp) for the corresponding **tooltip** (on hover). See ["Willing to become a vassal" and "vassal" icons](/README.md#willing-to-become-a-vassal-and-vassal-icons-in-foreign-advisors-glance-tab).
+- Cap **maximum number of players per page** in the **Glance Tab** (e.g., max 16 players per page gives 3 pages at SAS48 Worldsize (if all players are known)), with **clickable left and right arrows for navigation**. Fixes **issue of Glance Tab clipping horizontally** if more than 24 players are known and columns being too tight. Last page visited is **remembered and resumed from** on Glance Tab next opening. Diagonal player-vs-itself cells are now left empty instead of showing incorrect/inconsistent `+0` attitude display; see [KI#140](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#140---fixed-base-advciv-issue-foreign-advisor-glance-tab-showed-incorrect-and-inconsistent-0-attitude-display-in-self-cells). See also [KI#134](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#134---fixed-base-advciv-issue-foreign-diplomacy-advisor-glance-tab-column-icons-overflow-horizontally-with-24-rival-players).
+- Reworked the **Military Advisor** in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) now with Unit Combat and Units **icons**. Note: **unit icon size** is **increased** at **higher resolutions** (e.g., from 24 to 32 if resolution height >= 1440), and **promotion icon size** is **increased** (no longer DLL-hardcoded (was 16)). **Lift up the unit panel to full height** (reduces the need for scrolling vertically) and **expand it laterally** to **accommodate lengthy unit rows** (e.g., avoid line wrap if unit name is long, if there are many promotions). Make **show/hide individual unit text clickable** too (more accessible than the small +/- button alone). **Increase leader icon bar from 1 to multiple rows**, and **do not reduce icon size until all rows are full**. For example, at 1080p, 5 rows allow to show up to 45 players (including barbarian) at full leader icon size before leader icon size is reduced. **Reduce Leader icon size reduction** when all rows are full (**mild reduction**, no longer halved). See also [KI#123](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#123---fixed-bug-domesticmilitary-advisor-variant-toggles-required-restarting-civ4), [KI#130](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#130---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-unit-rows-showing-build-player-name-instead-of-improvement-text-military-advisor-map-tab), and [KI#131](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#131---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-live-unit-build-action-text-not-being-space-separated-from-its-turn-timer). Note 2: as of now the [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) is not supported.
+- Added a new **Battles tab** in the Military Advisor, showing as a **sortable table** the detailed **record of each battle** for the selected player in debug dropdown (or the active player or its vassals outside debug mode): **Turn**, **Year**, **Result** (Won, Lost, Retreat) as emoji, **Estimated Odds %** (simple starting effective strength comparison, not exact Civ4 combat odds), **Role** (Are we the attacker?) as emoji, **base Strength** (XML), **start effective Strength** (including modifiers at that battle), **end effective Strength**, **max effective Strength**, **XP before combat** (yellow if Great-General-led), **Our Unit**, **Their Unit** (unit name in yellow if Great-General-led), **same** strength/XP columns for their unit, **Civ icon**, **Player icon**, **Player ID** (to cover the same leader picked by several leaders (custom games, etc.)), **Captured Unit type**, **Captured Unit icon**, **Hill or Peak icon**, **Terrain icon**, **Feature icon**, **Click Plot icon** (**on click camera is moved to this plot** (as the wonder tabs' (Info Screen) text does), with distinct art for normal plot, defended city, and captured city battles). Icons are **hoverable to sevopedia** (or have a camera effect). **Text color** is added for Result (Won: green; Lost: red; Retreat: yellow), effective Strength (white: 100%, green: > 66%, yellow: > 33%; red <= 33%), and captured units (we gained a unit amount: green; we lost a unit amount: red). Implemented a **legend link**, and **LOG Button** (as the Timeline tab). Examples of LOG: `163 | 760 AD | Lost | 43 | A | 6 | 6.04 |  | 7.20 | 8 | 0 | Camel Archer | Longbowman | 5 | 0 | 4 | 8.10 | 5.04 | 9.00 | 9 | 0 |  |  | TERRAIN_GRASS |  | 54 | 30`, `133 | 10 BC | Won | 64 | A | 3 | 3.30 | 1.81 | 3.30 | 2 | 0 | Trireme | Galley | 1 | 0 | 2 | 1.84 |  | 2.20 | 48 | 0 |  |  | TERRAIN_COAST |  | 32 | 10`. Main files changed: [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py), [SASBattleHistory.py](/Assets/Python/SASBattleHistory.py), [CvEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/CvEventManager.py), [BugEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/BugEventManager.py), [CvUnit.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvUnit.cpp), [CvDllPythonEvents.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDllPythonEvents.cpp), [CvDllPythonEvents.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDllPythonEvents.h), [CvEventReporter.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEventReporter.cpp), [CvEventReporter.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEventReporter.h).
+- Added a new **Summary tab** in the Military Advisor, showing a **synthetic view** of our Military: **Support** (detailed Cost and Supply, and Unit Cap numerical breakdown (e.g., `P x R x M    (1 x 100 x 82) / 10000 = 0 gold icon char`), Military Buildings, Military Production (some not shown for concision as panel is mostly full) and XP information, and Allied Hammers for total hammer value of allies' (e.g., vassals, same team) army); **Army** (detailed numerical overview for military/civilian units, Domain repartition (Land/Sea/Air), Strongest, Costliest, Total/Avg Hammers as a power estimation of units, Power Rank (Known) (e.g., `9/11` (in fact `44/48` if debug mode is enabled for spoilers)), Top promotions, Covert Units (Invisible, Spies, Hidden Nationality), And upgradeable units costs (Min/Avg/Max/Total)); **Deployment** (Allied/Neutral/Enemy Cities/Territory/Roaming information with Avg Defense and Best defense of our cities, defensive buildings (as of now Walls and Castles (e.g., `1 / 2`)), Wounded information (Max/Avg/Min and Full/High/Medium/Low Health (e.g, `15 (100%)`)), and Battles reusing the [SASBattleHistory.py](/Assets/Python/SASBattleHistory.py) added with the new Battles Tab (Won/Retreated/Lost (e.g., `35 (33%)`)), Good-Luck Wins and Bad-Luck Losses counts (`e.g., 11 (31%)`), Best/Worst (e.g., `6.3 vs 10.0 1300 AD (39%)`)). Also added a **legend link**.
+- Added a new **Composition Tab**, as a set of **sortable tables** for **Current** (unlike saved data in the Statistics Tab in the Info Screen) **Units** (non-civilian, including Animal (including Barbarian in debug mode)), **Promotions**, and **Unit Combats** **counts**, default-**sorted from most to least** for no tedium (as done in the Statistics Tab). See also [KI#129](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#129---fixed-military-advisor-map-tab-minimap-disappeared-after-switching-tabs).
+- Similarly Beautified and Enhanced the **Technology Advisor** in [CvTechChooser.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechChooser.py) so it uses more of the screen while still preserving key information. Players can **optionally** set an **alternative lower right space for scoreboard** on **lower game resolutions** (e.g., 1920*1080) so that an **extra column or more is visible** in the technology advisor, and an **alternative top space space** for **advisor buttons** (in map view) because this alternative right space may cover these advisor buttons. **Boldened title** for consistency. See also [KI#114](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#114---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-tech-advisor-on-save-load-initially-shown-current-tech-missing-turns-left-timer-until-another-tech-is-clicked). Shifted the **default horizontal tech-tree start position** left so, at 1080p, the current visible Ancient-era last column renders fully and symmetrically instead of being partially cut off to the right, and without having to tediously nudge the horizontal scrollbar at game start. **When opening** Technology Advisor, **right-align scoreboard leader text** so it is easier to read (because text is often not visible due to advisor width expansion). **On Technology Advisor close**, it **reverts back** to usual alignment.
 - **Inverted BUG Options** for the **Technology Advisor** and the **Religion Advisor** so they are more accessible. They are now **enabled as a default**, and ticking their box disables them. Rewrote their text for clarity (e.g. "GP Research" -> **"Hide bulbing indicators"**). See [Inverted BUG options](/README.md#inverted-bug-options).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5718+) New **World Advisor**: shows **detailed BFC, suburbs, and territory geography** information as **sortable tables**. BFC tabs show **counts per city (rows) and per field (columns)**, and have a **click to enter city button** (similar to the Info Screen's Wonders tab). The BFC1 tab shows mostly **plot type** (Peak, Hill, Water, Land) and other information (**River, Lake, Coastal Land, sortable City found year and population**) and **Terrains/Features** information; the BFC2 tab shows mostly **Bonuses** and **Improvements** with other information (**Routes**). The Territory tab shows a **condensed count summary** with 4 tables of the former BFC tabs, with a BFC, suburbs (i.e. plots outside BFC), and **total columns** for each field (rows), **total fields (rows)** for each table, **hover support** and **pedia redirect on click** (if a corresponding pedia page exists), and a legend link. Note: totals are not the strict sum of all rows as some may overlap (e.g., river and hill). The **environment tab** is now part of the World advisor (better thematic fit).
-- Did a similar rework of the **Info Screen** in [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py); in particular in **Top 5 Cities** we now use a multilist to display more wonders in a prettier way, and in the **Wonders** tab we now **show the Wonders' Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the first column (**click to move to city** mechanic is moved to the City column instead); the **Statistics** tab now also shows buttons (plus **change default ordering** from alphabetical to **from most to least Built** (avoids tedious manual user ordering each time)), and the **Graph** Tab and possibly other tabs also show buttons (e.g., **leader icons before text**, **emojis**). Also added other information (e.g., turn numbers in the Graph tab). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5718+) **Removed** the **Improvements table** from the Statistics tab, because it was **inconsistent** with how Units and Buidings show all-time total **built**, Improvements would only show **current** possession (e.g., building a farm, replacing it with a cottage, then replacing it again with a farm would be Current 1 farm, not total built 2 farms), plus the World Advisor is a **better thematic fit**.
